  "worked_solution": "We have $\\frac{1}{10}$ on the left and $\\frac{7}{10}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129500/assets/c40da91dc3f57bf93f7e1fac3d7816ee4b534ad74ce71005ec3fbf0f6825910c.png)\n\nThe shape on the left has $1$ shaded piece, and the shape on the right has $7$ shaded pieces. So the number of shaded pieces has increased by a factor of $7.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{10}\\times 7=\\frac{7}{10}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $7.$",
